# Keep the published package free of local working copies.
#
# Why this file exists at all: `package.json` lists `"lib"` in `files`, and a
# DIRECTORY entry in `files` wins over `.gitignore`. Thirteen editor backups
# (`.bak-*`, ~4.1 MB) therefore rode along into the tarball - 74% of the
# published unpacked size - even though `.gitignore` already excluded them and
# git never tracked them. The `.gitignore` rule was doing the opposite of what
# it looked like it was doing.
#
# So the exclusion is declared where npm actually reads it. This is a second
# line of defence, not the only one: the backups are also no longer kept inside
# `lib/` at all (they live in the workspace, outside the package root).
#
# Patterns mirror `.gitignore`; a comment on each says why it is here.

# Working copies made while editing
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.orig-*
*.rej

# Temp files from the write-temp-then-rename pattern used by the ledgers
*.tmp

# Local runtime state the plugin writes next to itself (never published)
.workbuddy-xdpool/
pool-status.json
pool-settings.json
disabled-accounts.json
paused-accounts.json
sticky-sessions.json
guard-status.json
prompt.json
automation.json
models.json
launcher.log
.needs-reinstall
accounts/
secrets/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
